# javac writes its command line to javac.<timestamp>.args in the working directory whenever
# that line is too long for the OS, and leaves the file behind. Gradle never produces one -
# it keeps its own argfiles under build/ - but CLAUDE.md documents building this module by
# hand with javac against org.robolectric:android-all, because dl.google.com is unreachable
# from the Claude Code sandbox and ./gradlew cannot run there. Two of these were committed
# that way, carrying absolute /tmp paths from the machine that made them.
javac.*.args

# Local-only JVM test jars fetched by tools/run-jvm-tests.sh (JUnit, org.json).
tools/lib/
tools/build/
